Description:
At Inhibrx, our mission is to deliver optimized, biologic therapeutics to people with life-threatening conditions. Toward this goal, we have built a large and diverse pipeline with the potential to impact cancer and orphan diseases through our single domain antibody platform technology. Single domain antibodies (sdAbs) provide a small, simple, modular target binding domain that can be combined in a variety of ways to meet specific needs of unique biological targets. Our sdAb-based therapeutic candidates have been designed to interface with the biology of each target antigen, and can be readily manufactured at high yields with established processes. We have created various multivalent and multispecific therapeutic formats that are each designed to achieve unique functions, including the ability to:

- effectively cluster receptors with precisely defined valency;
- simultaneously engage multiple antigens or epitopes;
- combine synergistic functions in a single molecule; and
- restrict therapeutic activity to the tumor microenvironment or other biologically distinct tissue.

We provide Next-Generation Sequencing library synthesis, sequencing and bioinformatic support using the ‘ClickSeq‘1 method of NGS library synthesis. 

ClickSeq is a unique method for RNAseq and DNAseq that uses ‘Click-Chemistry’ in place of commonly used biological reagents such as fragmentases and ligases. ClickSeq is a very simple procedure and considerably cheaper than other commonly used alternatives. 

-No Fragmentation;
-No ligation;
-Highly scalable;
-Ultra-low artifactual chimera formation1;
-Specialized Transcriptomic applications;
-Integrated analysis pipelines, from RNA to results;
-Affordable library synthesis;
-RNA or DNA
-Suitable for fragmented/degraded samples

New Feed Team is a recent and dynamic company born from 30 years’ experience in production of feed additives and premixes destinated for all animal species. 
As its originating company, N.F.T. is highly specialized in solutions for:
-	The preservation of qualitative characteristics of feed using liquid or powder preservatives;
-	The optimization of digestive processes and feed efficacy through acidifiers;
-	The prevention against detrimental effects due to toxins (mycotoxins+endotoxins) using tailor-made binders.
-	The oil/ fat protection in raw ingredients and feeds through natural and synthetic antioxidants.

Simpatica Medicine, Inc. is a precision medicine company that partners with hospitals and clinicians to guide the use of today’s powerful new immunologic and cellular therapies for their patients.

Simpatica Medicine, Inc. is based in San Francisco.

@SimpaticaMed on Twitter

Bluechiip, a Cryonix Group Brand, is a leader in the development of advanced sample management solutions, understands that every biological sample is critical, so our objective is to manage each one with optimal quality in the most efficient way. Bluechiip provides a range of products and services across clinical research, drug development and advanced cell therapies to support the world’s leading laboratories across pharmaceutical, biotech and academic institutes globally.

Bluechiip’s Advanced Sample Management Solution and patented technology stack operates across all, extreme (from –196°C to +150°C) temperatures, enabling unmatched accuracy, traceability, and real-time data capture at the individual sample level. Its integrated system of enabled cryogenic vials, smart readers, and cloud-based software delivers a fully digitized sample management workflow - eliminating manual data entry, improving regulatory compliance, and dramatically increasing productivity.

Key advantages of Bluechiip product offerings include:
# True cold-chain tracking from storage to bench, with live sample temperature and location data;
# Plug-and-play compatibility with existing workflows and digital tools (e.g. ELN, LIMS);
# Rapid deployment without the need for custom software or IT infrastructure;
# Scalable and cost-efficient alternative to fully automated freezer systems; and
# Enhanced traceability and security for critical assets in biobanking, cell therapy, IVF, clinical trials, and pharma R&D.

Please note that this page now reflects the assets and brand of Bluechiip under the ownership by Cryonix Group. Previous company roles listed here may not reflect current affiliations. For more information, refer to the Cryonix Group page.

The Crop Bioengineering Center (CBC) strives to be a global leader in efficient precision crop breeding using innovative and transformative genome engineering technologies. The CBC is

(1) a scientific platform that inspires, promotes and supports interdisciplinary, collaborative interaction among natural scientists, social scientists, humanists and engineers in the innovative development and application of crop genome engineering technologies;

(2) a technology center that provides expertise and service in genome engineering to enable the crop research community in the areas of gene discovery, functional analysis and crop improvement;

(3) a knowledge and information hub that engages, communicates with and educates the public with regard to biotechnology advances, regulatory implications and policy development in the area of crop bioengineering.

The Antibody Society is an international, non profit trade association representing individuals and organizations involved in antibody related research and development. The Society has a variety of initiatives and working groups focused on improving the antibody field.

We are:
- Creating opportunities for education and networking;
- Monitoring and reporting advances in the commercial pipeline for antibody and CAR-T therapeutics;
- Creating standards for characterizing antibody and T-cell receptor repertoires, and engaging this field;
- Engaging government and international agencies on matters concerning the antibody community.

We encourage you to join the 2,700+ members of The Antibody Society to take advantage of the substantial benefits of membership, including discounts on fees for selected Informa Connect, CHI, and Hanson Wade meetings and access to information in the Members Only section of the website. In particular, we encourage members to take advantage of the discount on registration for Antibody Engineering & Therapeutics, which is the annual meeting of The Antibody Society traditionally held in San Diego in December.

Membership is free for students, post docs and employees of our corporate sponsors.

